-### APK only
+### In the app only
 
 The public ADS-B aggregators serve data to anyone and CORS headers to nobody: adsb.lol
 and adsb.fi answer a command-line request and fail in a browser, airplanes.live and
@@ -340,14 +340,14 @@ adsb.one answer 403, OpenSky allows only its own origin, and the public CORS pro
 either time out or rate-limit long before an 8-second poll. A static site has nothing to
 call.
 
-The APK is not a browser. Capacitor's native HTTP makes the request in Java, where the
-same-origin rule does not apply, so the app calls the feed directly — no proxy, nothing
+The Android and iPhone/iPad apps are not browsers. Capacitor's native HTTP makes the request
+in native code (Java on Android, Swift on iOS), where the same-origin rule does not apply, so the app calls the feed directly — no proxy, nothing
 hosted. **In a browser the Traffic box is still there but dimmed**, with the reason on it:
 a control that vanishes between the phone and the desktop makes you wonder what else moved.
 Only `featureLiveTraffic` removes it.
 
 `featureLiveTraffic` in the tuning gist decides whether the feature exists. It is **on** in
-the live app — the Traffic box is there, dimmed in a browser and live in the APK.
+the live app — the Traffic box is there, dimmed in a browser and live in the apps.
 
